119"},{"content_hash":"e24efdc8cef67198fcf7d59e03ca795922cf1b036b49c96b3ea26840d42cab5d","event_uuid":"ce801f11-59fb-4244-9332-43c85bddba69","position":{"commit_sha":"48caca6de84a9a8019694c6f289a87d5d8e45f28","position":"1795212312597721001-ce801f11-59fb-4244-9332-43c85bddba69"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"flaky","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Deterministic reproduction and fix evidence (2026-11-19, PST).\n\n**Reproduction (AC1).** macOS, git 2.56.0. Two DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES interposers: one pauses the commit's detached `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach` child at its opendir of `.git/worktrees`; the other pauses `git worktree add -q --detach <repo>/.tickets-tracker` right after its mkdir of `.git/worktrees/-tickets-tracker`. Releasing the maintenance child inside the add's window:\n- test's commit as written: 3/3 runs `rc=128 fatal: could not open '.git/worktrees/-tickets-tracker/locked' for writing: No such file or directory`\n- commit with `-c maintenance.auto=false`: 3/3 rc=0\n- commit with `GIT_TEST_MAINT_AUTO_DETACH=false` (the fix): the maintenance scan is reached while the commit is still running; the paused add then survives, 3/3 rc=0\n- `git maintenance run --auto --no-detach` run inside the paused window also reproduces the exact error.\nCommit's child argv: default `['git','maintenance','run','--auto','--quiet','--detach']`; with the switch `[... '--no-detach']`.\nGit source (v2.56.1, unchanged on master): builtin/worktree.c:505 mkdir, :526-530 writes `locked`; worktree.c should_prune_worktree returns \"gitdir file does not exist\" with no expiry check; default unscheduled strategy is geometric, which includes worktree-prune.\n\n**Change** (commit 316a1909e26, worktree fix-test-git-maint-detach). Implementation notes against the plan, from the plan-review advisories:\n- The guard protection is a positive control instead of an os.environ probe: `_git_upkeep.assert_git_detaches_by_default` makes an unpinned control commit and requires a `--detach` child, so it sees what git actually saw. `assert_no_detached_upkeep` calls it, and `test_init_leaves_no_detached_upkeep` (which does not use that helper) calls it directly from its fixture.\n- Git version: the switch exists from git 2.47, where auto-maintenance first put `--detach`/`--no-detach` on the child argv. On an older git (floor 2.38) the variable is ignored; the control and the new test skip there with the reason, because no `--detach` is observable. The worktree-prune race needs the worktree-prune maintenance task, which is newer still.\n- Limit: a test that starts git with an env mapping built from scratch (not from os.environ) does not get the switch.\n\n**Pre-fix result of the new test:** with origin/main's conftest, `test_a_raw_commit_runs_its_maintenance_in_the_foreground` fails: `a test's raw git commit left detached maintenance running: [['git', 'maintenance', 'run', '--auto', '--quiet', '--detach']]`. With the fix: 3 passed. The 4 guards plus test_recent_creates_shared_journal, test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars, test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev, test_authorship_fixture_maintenance, test_topology_template_upkeep_guard, test_bare_clone_source_upkeep_sweep: 72 passed, 1 error; the error is the repo-isolation HEAD watchdog (`git rev-parse HEAD` timed out after 5 s, 3 attempts) at host load average 43, the same failure as closed bug dominating-removable-monkfish.","timestamp":1795151804820589001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local verify evidence for Gerrit 3478 (found by the verify-parity sweep, not acted on): the sandboxed make verify of worktree fix-test-git-maint-detach at b6b714ca03d (log .rebar/worktrees/fix-test-git-maint-detach/.rebar/scratch/s05f74084/make-verify.log) failed tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py::test_all_non_fixture_subprocess_environments_use_the_safe_boundary with assert ['tests/_git_upkeep.py:215'] == []. That line passes env=subprocess_env(GIT_TRACE2_EVENT=...) in the detach-control commit. This is a deterministic policy-scan failure, not a load or sandbox effect; check whether the current 3478 patch set still carries it before Submit.","timestamp":1795206516539148001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit 3478, merged 6f09daf873a (confirmed on origin/main). Gate: LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved, submitted revision-scoped. make verify via verify-slot.sh, run outside the agent sandbox on origin/main e7532d2b71c (contains 3477, 3478, 3480): rc=0, 21543 passed / 31 skipped, integration tier 226 passed / 2 skipped (2026-11-20 12:31-13:36 PST). Earlier sandboxed runs on the patch sets were red with load and sandbox failures outside the changed code; the one change-related failure (3478 patch set 1: test_subprocess_env_repr_security, tests/_git_upkeep.py:215) was fixed in patch set 2.","timestamp":1795210822610398001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1795058895572871123,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1d14cf1a-e506-456d-b26a-f426c6c3d96d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"44b2-e70e-2b9f-4d2a"},{"link_uuid":"bdbb6916-2412-46b4-ad60-4e6e33cd5a40","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"},{"link_uuid":"ab4976f0-4c1d-4f14-ba5a-d73c5c5ac657","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"62f1-7e72-8f28-4937"},{"link_uuid":"012414c4-61be-4217-be56-83840a5f6eea","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"87ff-e0a0-dd37-4edb"}],"description":"## Observation\nGerrit 3440 patch set 1 (9771ff17b27) got `Verified -1` from run 44445060532, job 135298967486 (`build-and-test / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.12)`, git 2.56.1, 2026-11-19). The only failure was `tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py::test_a_linked_worktree_tracker_keeps_the_journal_in_its_own_git_dir` (`:196-212`): the setup command `git worktree add -q --detach <tmp>/repo/.tickets-tracker` exited 128 with `fatal: could not open '.git/worktrees/-tickets-tracker/locked' for writing: No such file or directory`. The change under test does not touch this test or the code it exercises (op-cert key loading, the comment-echo cleanup script, docs, the Windows sweep workflow). The module passed 5 of 5 times locally on macOS.\n\nThe repo is a fresh `git init` under the test's own `tmp_path`, so nothing else should touch its `.git/worktrees/`. git writes `locked` right after creating `.git/worktrees/<id>/`; ENOENT means that directory was gone or never created at that path.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n- A concurrent `git worktree prune` against this repo (callers: `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:186`, `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py:304`), reached through an inherited `GIT_DIR`/cwd from a detached child of an earlier test on the same xdist worker.\n- A git 2.56.x worktree-id sanitisation issue for a dot-led basename (`.tickets-tracker` becomes `-tickets-tracker`).\n\n## Root cause (reproduced deterministically on 2026-11-19)\nNeither hypothesis holds. The pruner is a detached `git maintenance run --auto` that the test's own setup `git commit` starts, one step before its `git worktree add`.\n\n- `git commit` ends by starting `git maintenance run --auto --detach`, a child that outlives the commit (`run-command.c:prepare_auto_maintenance`; detaching is the default when neither `maintenance.autoDetach` nor `gc.autoDetach` is set).\n- Unscheduled maintenance now uses the `geometric` strategy, which includes the `worktree-prune` task (`builtin/gc.c`). Its auto condition and the `git worktree prune` it runs treat a `.git/worktrees/<id>/` directory holding neither `locked` nor `gitdir` as prunable (\"gitdir file does not exist\", with no expiry check: `worktree.c:should_prune_worktree`).\n- `git worktree add` creates that directory (`builtin/worktree.c:505`, v2.56.1) and writes `locked` (\"initializing\") only afterwards (`:526-530`). Git master has the same window. A maintenance run that scans in between deletes the in-flight directory, and the add dies writing `locked` with ENOENT.\n\nDeterministic reproduction (macOS, git 2.56.0, two `DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES` interposers in a scratch directory): pause the commit's detached maintenance child at its `opendir` of `.git/worktrees`, pause `git worktree add` right after its `mkdir` of `.git/worktrees/-tickets-tracker`, then release the maintenance child. 3 of 3 runs failed with exactly `fatal: could not open '.git/worktrees/-tickets-tracker/locked' for writing: No such file or directory`. The same sequence with the commit run as `git -c maintenance.auto=false commit` (no child) passed 3 of 3. Running `git maintenance run --auto --no-detach` inside the paused window also reproduces the error.\n\n## The class\nAny raw git write a test makes (commit, merge, fetch, a push into a local repository) leaves a detached auto-maintenance child running at git's defaults. 188 test files make a raw `git commit` and then create a linked worktree, directly or through `rebar init`. rebar's own git calls already keep maintenance off or in the foreground (`gitutil._IMPLICIT_MAINTENANCE_OFF`, the `_gc_config_unit` pins), so the exposure is the test suite's own git.\n\n## Approach\nDo what git's own test harness does: `t/test-lib.sh` exports `GIT_TEST_MAINT_AUTO_DETACH=false` with the comment \"Ensure that tests cannot race with background maintenance by default.\" In `tests/conftest.py`'s `pytest_configure`, after the existing `scrub_ambient_git_config`, set `GIT_TEST_MAINT_AUTO_DETACH=false` in `os.environ` for the session (xdist workers and every test subprocess inherit it). Git reads it only when neither `maintenance.autoDetach` nor `gc.autoDetach` is configured. The triggered maintenance still runs, but in the foreground of the command that started it, so it finishes before that command returns. Any repo-local or global pin a test sets keeps precedence, and `GIT_CONFIG_*`, which the scrub keeps clean, is untouched. This is a setting of git's existing variable inside the test harness; it adds no rebar config key, environment variable, or flag.\n\nGuard tests that prove a pin prevents `--detach` need git's default of detaching, or they pass without testing anything:\n- `tests/_git_upkeep.py`: `assert_no_detached_upkeep` fails with a clear message if `GIT_TEST_MAINT_AUTO_DETACH` is `false` when it runs, so a guard that forgets to restore git's default cannot pass vacuously.\n- Delete the variable (`monkeypatch.delenv`) for the guards' own runs: `tests/unit/test_init_leaves_no_detached_upkeep.py`, `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py`, `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py`.\n- `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev.py` and `tests/unit/test_authorship_fixture_maintenance.py` stay unchanged: they write `autoDetach = true` into a global config, which outranks the variable.\n\nRejected alternatives: injecting `maintenance.auto=false` through `GIT_CONFIG_*` (it outranks the repo-local pins the guards exist to test, and the scrub exists to keep that channel clean); per-file fixes (188 files, and the next new test reopens the class).\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/conftest.py`\n- `tests/_git_upkeep.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_init_leaves_no_detached_upkeep.py`\n- `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_suite_git_maintenance_foreground.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n- New `tests/unit/test_suite_git_maintenance_foreground.py`: in a fresh repository, a raw `git commit` under `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` records a `git maintenance run` child (positive control: the commit did trigger maintenance), and no recorded child carries `--detach`. This is a fact about the recorded argv, with no timing. It fails on the pre-fix tree, where the child is `--detach`, and passes with the fix.\n- A second case covers the guard's failure path: `assert_no_detached_upkeep` raises when the variable is `false`.\n- Rerun the scratch reproduction with the session's setting instead of `-c maintenance.auto=false`: the commit's maintenance reaches its worktree scan before the commit returns, and the paused `git worktree add` succeeds.\n- The 4 guard files, `tests/unit/test_recent_creates_shared_journal.py`, and `tests/unit/test_compact_trigger_shared_sidecars.py` pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The interleaving or condition that produces the ENOENT is reproduced deterministically and recorded here.\n- [x] The test passes reliably under that condition, with the class fixed.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_suite_git_maintenance_foreground.py` fails on the pre-fix tree and passes with the fix (checked by running it on both trees; results recorded here).\n- [x] `make verify` passes on the change.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"session GIT_TEST_MAINT_AUTO_DETACH=false"},{"path":"tests/_git_upkeep.py","reason":"guard refuses to run without git default detach"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_init_leaves_no_detached_upkeep.py","reason":"restore git default detach for the guard"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py","reason":"restore git default detach for the guard"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py","reason":"restore git default detach for the guard"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py","reason":"restore git default detach for the guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_suite_git_maintenance_foreground.py","reason":"regression test for foreground maintenance"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","62f1-7e72-8f28-4937"],["relates_to","87ff-e0a0-dd37-4edb"],["relates_to","8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a223f305-4e1a-4581-ac08-90489f7f47de","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["flaky"],"ticket_id":"7fcc-dac7-6f05-4ad1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_a_linked_worktree_tracker_keeps_the_journal_in_its_own_git_dir: `git worktree add` intermittently fails on its own .git/worktrees lock file","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cd952f48-a28c-4672-8b6a-43c7cecc28b5","b1b3c6ed-aab9-47f2-84f5-5c88df7c42a9","bdbb6916-2412-46b4-ad60-4e6e33cd5a40","d2fc85df-199d-4f83-b055-0c3f0c9b9bd6","3aa03d6f-a74b-4119-96fa-0f3d44287c1c","7a036cc4-ce25-4db8-a97d-a7b1136efb32","59ebf4ed-b304-4ea3-bea6-ef78a485a18a","ab4976f0-4c1d-4f14-ba5a-d73c5c5ac657","012414c4-61be-4217-be56-83840a5f6eea","2a914fed-cfa5-4e1b-a42d-a951467f1df9","38c50c41-ac00-4eea-8abc-de7684523983","c323e873-eb79-4690-962b-54727481725e","a223f305-4e1a-4581-ac08-90489f7f47de","ce801f11-59fb-4244-9332-43c85bddba69"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795212312597721002,"uuid":"496aa340-92bf-406c-a413-ca9ed450d34e"}